From: Asuka <asuka@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-amsa26zp01: fix brightness glitch and idle restore

Do not rewrite WRCTRLD (0x53) on every backlight tick. That DCS during
live DSC video garbles the panel.

Leave smooth dimming off (0x53 = 0x20) in the on-sequence. With 0x28 the
panel ramps WRDISBV down for GNOME idle-dim, then ignores the later
increase so typing/touch never restores; the slider still works because
it writes a new value after the ramp is idle.

Skip WRDISBV only when the panel is unprepared. ctx->panel.prepared is
valid with both drm_panel_init (6.17) and devm_drm_panel_alloc (7.2.0).

Do not set MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM on this video-mode DSC panel: LP commands
during active video can leave the panel black.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amsa26zp01.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amsa26zp01.c
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(dsi_ctx, 50);
 	// #define SAMSUNG_BRIGHTNESS_MODE	0x53
 	// mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, SAMSUNG_BRIGHTNESS_MODE, 0xE0);
-	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_WRITE_CONTROL_DISPLAY, 0x28);  /* 0x20:Normal mode + Smooth dimming off; 0x28: Normal mode + Smooth dimming on */
+	/* 0x20: BCTRL on, smooth dimming off so idle-undim WRDISBV applies immediately */
+	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, MIPI_DCS_WRITE_CONTROL_DISPLAY, 0x20);
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0xf8, 0x58, 0x00, 0x30, 0x35);
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(dsi_ctx, 100);
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0xf9, 0xc0, 0x2b);
@@ -172,12 +173,13 @@
 static int samsung_amsa26zp01_bl_update_status(struct backlight_device *bl)
 {
 	struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi = bl_get_data(bl);
+	struct samsung_amsa26zp01 *ctx = mipi_dsi_get_drvdata(dsi);
 	u16 brightness = backlight_get_brightness(bl);
 	int ret;
-	// u8 payload_hbm_on[1] = { 0xE0 };	/* HBM Mode */
-	// u8 payload_hbm_off[1] = { 0x28 }; /* 0x20:Normal mode + Smooth dimming off; 0x28: Normal mode + Smooth dimming on */
-	struct mipi_dsi_multi_context dsi_ctx = { .dsi = dsi };
-	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x53, 0x28);
+
+	/* WRCTRLD during video-mode DSC scanout glitches the panel. */
+	if (!ctx->panel.prepared)
+		return 0;
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(dsi, brightness);
 	if (ret < 0)
